description.to:
Produce the first citable corpus baseline as an immutable contract-versioned four-layer artifact.

Specify schema, rendering, computability states, and readiness gates first. Migration audits may report legacy, unscorable, or incomplete populations, but they are not baseline series 1.

Series 1 freezes only after the canonical harness and gold migration land and the readiness command verifies:

- zero accepted legacy or source-token-only identities;
- canonical accepted flow coverage meeting approved count and packet-diversity thresholds;
- reviewed packet/layer scopes;
- acceptable path-contract and unscorable rates;
- validated materializations and fingerprint inputs.

Series 1 records `predecessor: none`; no trustworthy prior scanner baseline exists. Subsequent contract/gold series bridge against the same scanner commit, while detector changes compare to but never overwrite a frozen series.

Definition of done: committed canonical JSON plus deterministic Markdown, full fingerprint and readiness evidence, CI validation, and a clean series-1 freeze that refuses incomplete four-layer input.
